The "pushed PC for the trap" turns out to be irrelevant to the SR1
recovery process. All the information is in SR0, SR1 and SR2. MMU SR2
has the restart PC. The "pushed PC" can be thrown away.

A compatible recovery process for the cases we've seen so far, except
for two E11 cases, would be:

1.  Use SR0 to locate the faulting page. Map it.
2.  Apply all SR1 inc/decs to the appropriate saved registers.
    (R7 inc/decs may be made, but they will be discarded with
     the next step).
3.  Restart the instruction at the location specified by SR2

(And this is also how the KDJ11-A manual describes the process).

In TEST05 futher below SimH records the PC movement from 100000 to
100002 with [27] in SR1. J11 advances the PC, but leaves SR1 as [0]. 
