Maybe you didn't know this, but TU58s aren't really tapes. They only
*look* like tapes when humans look at them. When the software looks at
them (from the OS, and to an extent the boot ROM), they are random
access block addressable devices, same as disks are (a bit smaller and
a bit slower and a LOT cheaper, than disk, in their day). TU56
DECtapes worked similarly to the TU58 (taking a high level view), as
random access disk-like devices, although the mechanics and the
interface were (obviously) different.


