I'm well aware of that, however the technique is commonplace in RT-11
for the simple cases. As I said, I use the non-returning trap handler
technique for RTI, RETURN etc. Actually, the main problem with the
RT-11 technique is that you can mask other traps. Anyway, I had to
move all the tests to the trap handler yesterday when I finally put
the condition code tracking in.

<snip>
>>>> Architectures are not retrospective, they are working specifications
>>>> of new implementations. The point I'm making about the PDP-11 is that
>>>> it didn't stick to the architecture (unless you reduce the term
>>>> "architecture" to something very fuzzy, almost aspirational).
>>>
>>> And I disagree. The different PDP-11s were not implemented out of a blue
>>> sky, but did actually follow some principles defined way back in 1969.
>>> The PDP-11 architecture.
>>> If they didn't follow that, then the machines would not have been
>>> usable. There is a reason why RT-11 and RSX will work on all different
