TEST21:: MFPS
I've added a 4-character condition code field, e.g. "NZVC", (and I've
edited the earlier examples above).

MFPS instruction tests fail because the condition codes pushed by the
abort trap have been modified from the original. In the examples ----
is pushed as -Z-- and NZVC is pushed as ---C. The restarted
instruction will return the wrong condition codes. This is not good.

J11/SimH:
Test21: mfps (r0)+
Before: R0=100000 SP=742 PC=6526 PS=30000 ----
After:  R0=100001 SP=742 PC=6530 PS=30004 -Z--
        Vec=250 SR0=100011 SR1=[0|10] SR2=6526

Before: R0=100000 SP=742 PC=6526 PS=30017 NZVC
After:  R0=100001 SP=742 PC=6530 PS=30001 ---C
        Vec=250 SR0=100011 SR1=[0|10] SR2=6526

The changes being applied to the PS are those described for the
instruction. In the case of MFPS:

  N: set if PS <0> = 1; cleared otherwise
  Z: set if PS <07:00> = 0; cleared otherwise
  V: cleared
  C: not affected

MTPS does not have a problem.

BTW: Perhaps it's time to note the obvious: The J11 and SimH tend to
apply the side-affects of an operation as an instruction progresses
where E11 tends wait until an instruction has completed before
applying side-affects. And it's also clear that the SimH attempts to
get as close as possible to the J11's operational behavior, so any
deviations from J11 behavior are probably worth reporting.

I did a final compare of the J11 and SimH, clearing some details etc.
The results are in the source of the utility.






Ian


