When the IBM PC first came out, there were stories that
setting the wrong sweep frequencies could destroy the
monitor. 

Most now are multisync, and can figure out if they are
given a frequency that they can't handle, but not all of them.

In the mainframe (washing machine sized) disk days, there were
stories about finding the seek pattern that would hit a
resonance in the system, possibly destroying an expensive
disk drive. I don't know any personally that did, though.

-- glen


