Both the monochrome and CGA, the two available for the original
PC, use the 6845 CRT controller. All the timing is specified
by programmed registers. In character mode, it knows how to
count character lines, and scan lines within a character,
all programmable.

I don't remember the details for later display cards, but
it is usual that the timing is done using programmable
registers.

