Yes. Not surprised, since all instructions in device drivers which 
happens between an interrupt, and the creation of the fork, for example, 
will be running at a raised IPL.
Also, if you search for ";;;", you also be getting a lot of empty lines, 
which is just because comments are running over several lines, and each 
line is prefixed with ;;;, if the code being commented is running at a 
raised IPL. But it's arguable how relevant empty lines with just a 
comment is...

Another nice point here is that device drivers structures are not being 
manipulated by more than one CPU, since a device can only be attached to 
one CPU at a time, so those pieces are the only ones where IPL is 
enough, and you don't have to worry about MP issues in RSX. The fork 
queue, however, is shared between all processors, and needs to be 
properly protected.

