I have been following Johnny's and Ian's discussion, but since I know
so little about the internals of RSX-11 and VMS, I have not commented.

This comment is only to note that I suggest a more careful look at
the code used for C$SISP.

 >Johnny Billquist wrote:

>>> I was looking in RMONFB.MAC.
>>> C$SIGN almost immediately do an EMT 374, which ends up in USR.
>>> What am I missing? 
>>
>> .CSIGEN (C$SIGN:) purges all channels before prompting for a new
>> command and opening files. Thus, it begins with a loop to purge
>> channels. Control is passed to the USR only if a *new* file is open on
>> a "special device", such as magtape or cassette. (In fact, "special
>> devices" have their own built-in ACPs and can be called without using
>> the USR, but that's a complication I've been avoiding introducing
>> here.)
>>
>> Note, .CSISPC (C$SISP:) does not purge or open files. 
>
> Must be looking at different versions of something, this is C$SIGN: 
> from RMONFB:
>
> .SBTTL  .CSIGEN AND .CSISPC - CSI CALL EMTS
>         .ENABL  LSB
> C$SIGN: CLR     R4
>         MOV     (PC)+,R0
>          .BYTE  8.,3
> 10$:    EMT     374
>         DECB    R0
>         BGE     10$
>         BR      11$
> C$SISP: MOV     #100000,R4
> 11$:    BIS     #CSIRN$,@R5
>         MOV     #CSI.$,R2
>         MOVB    JOBNUM,R3
>         BEQ     15$
>         BIS     #GTLIN$,@#JSW
> 15$:    TST     @R1
>         BEQ     20$
>         JMP     EMTUSR
> 20$:    INCB    R4
>         CMPB    USROWN,R3
>         BNE     30$
>         INCB    USRLVL
> CSIERR::CLRB    R4
>         BISB    USRLVL,R4
>         CALL    RIDUSR
> 30$:
>
>
> If I remember right, this is from RT-11 V5.5, so it might be that 
> things got changed after that?

If the code is inspected carefully, it can be seen that the
C$SISP sets a flag in R4 differently from the flag set in
R4 byC$SIGN.  In addition, the files on channels 0 to 8
are NOT purged prior to the common code starting at
label 11$:

At least that is my understanding of the above example.

Jerome Fine

