> If Johnny could please clarify, that would be helpful.
> I am only suggesting that I don't understand Johnny's
> response, but that I tend to conclude that Johnny's
> words mean that he thinks that both CSI routines
> do perform a .Purge loop. Ian and I have concluded
> that only .CSISPC (C$SISP:) performs the .Purge loop.

I have never made any distinction between various parts of the CSI, just 
noting that CSI calls USR.

Which is done both through an EMT 374 right at the start of C$SIGN, and 
later you have a "JMP  EMTUSR" (which would appear to happen for both).

And so, it would appear to me, that a call to CSI would block other USR 
calls, for the most part of the CSI processing.

	Johnny


