> RUST/SJ sub-directories, but it wasn't worth it.

Funny that you mention RTEM, since I seem to have come across a copy 
that I now have running on my RSX systems. It is weird, and I have not 
looked at all details. Also, a friend of mine have been doing most of 
the fooling around. He did get it to boot RT-11 V5.7 after a few patches 
to RT-11. Seems like RTEM got broken after V5.5 in the RT-11 side.

I don't know exactly how it works, but it uses a disk split into two 
parts. One is shared by all users, and holds all the normal binaries and 
stuff you'd expect, while the other part is your private disk, which 
holds all the rest of the stuff you do. But they are merged into one 
disk in the view of RT-11.

Also, it seems like the file protection is used, and all files on the 
shared part of the disk are protected, which seems like a wise thing. :-)


