The split disk looked kind of weird when I first saw it, but it makes a 
lot of sense. The actual system, as well as all the CUSPs then exist in 
only one copy on a system, even if you have lots of people running RTEM. 
All have their own private part of the disk where all their own files 
gets placed. Back when disks weren't that big, it would make a big 
difference, I suspect.
Nowadays, with terabyte disks, and RT-11 restricted to 32M, you can 
easily have as many full RT-11 disks as you care about, but with a 
system on one RM03, all you had was 63MB, for everything. (One RM03 is 
