V5.6 was the last release from DEC itself, so I would define V5.6 as
being in the final stages of RT-11's history. In fact, V5.6 had enough
significant new code to call it V6.0, but the RT-11 were trying to
keep a low profile within the company at the time. There wasn't a
great take-up of V5.6 IIRC, which is a pity because it was one of
their best releases. The audience was moving elsewhere.

