On the Windows server machine you do this:

C:> run c:\rust\she

o nf/detached		  ! start the Windows NF server
o define tmp c:\rust\tmp  !
o

On RT-11 or RUST you would do this:

. load nf
. assign nf tmp
. dir tmp:

The NF: driver is able to pick up the logical name TMP:. It sends this
name, along with a network request package to the server. 

The Windows server gets the name "tmp" and translates it locally to
get "c:\rust\tmp", a native directory, and sends back a RT-11-formate
directory to the RT-11/RUST system.

