aborted with the error code that you need to redo the system call again.
Which is the Unix solution to the problem.
Other systems instead backs out and redo the system call after it has 
been interrupted.

You seem to be pretty alone in thinking that you can just ignore it.

> There are rules which forbid one or two scenarios. For example, I
