the wait will be re-executed for you. There is no magic inside the 
kernel that resumes the wait. Simple and efficient. Re-execute the wait 
if interrupted. Since the wait-for calls have no context, there is 
nothing to back out, nothing that hurts from being redone, and it also 
automatically handles any changed conditions that might have happened as 
a part of the AST execution itself.

