Just in case you are interested, on a real DEC PDP-11/83, I generally find
that it takes about 240 seconds (4 minutes) to copy an RT-11 partition of
32 MB from one SCSI hard drive to another.  ESDI drives are about the
same and RD53 drives take over 300 seconds (5 minutes).

Under Ersatz-11 with synchronous I/O, it takes about 2 seconds on my
Pentium III running Windows 98SE and less than 1 second on a core 2 quad
at 2.8 GH running Windows XP.

I have probably mentioned these numbers before, but a 200 to 1 ratio is
quite impressive.  I imagine that with SATA III drives on even faster
systems, the ratio is even larger.

Jerome Fine


