The default settings for SimH and E11 are a 100 instruction delay for
console output.

E11:   show delay dl0   => 1:100.     (0:200. is for input)
SimH:  examine tto time => TIME 100

On a real PDP-11 DL11 terminal interface there is no additional delay
(unless output is suspended with ([ctrl/s]). Indeed, a good DLx11 is
double buffered so the first character completes immediately. The
following test counts instructions for four output characters. The
counts are in octal and need to be multipled by three (there are three
instructions in the counting loop).

     1st 2nd ...
DL11   1 144 144 144   Double-buffered (DLV11J actually)
SimH  42  42  42  42   Constant delay
E11   42  42  42  42   Constant delay
V11    1   1   1   1   "Ready" is immediate. Interrupt is delayed.

