SR0 are writeable. These bits are not writeable on the F11 or J11, but
a closer inspection of the 11/34 architecture documents indicates they
may well be writeable on a real 11/34, and that's the default E11 CPU.
I may have to find a different E11 test (see further below).

If anyone with an 11/34 is still reading this long post the test that
needs to be performed is something like this:

1000 012737  mov #177776,@#177572  ; see all in SR0 except MMU enable
1002 177776
1004 177572
1006 013700  mov @#177572,r0       ; get the result in R0
1010 177572
1012 000000  halt

The requisite result value will be in R0.

