The 11/34 architecture document 11/34 says that the state any SR0 bits
other than 0 and 8 are not meaningful if set by the user (but doesn't
say which can be set). In terms of the 11/34 architecture the state of
bits 5 and 6 is irrelevant if set by the user and thus neither E11 or
SimH is *architecturally* incorrect (or in "error") as the state is
"meaningless".

