Nope, and I'll try to resist as well :-)


I wrote a better SR1 testbed where all I need to for a new test is
fill in a template and insert the new test code.

Kernel and user memory are mapped the same space. Par5 is not mapped.
The tests are designed to fail at location 120000. An asterix marks
the part of the instruction which will cause the trap by trying to
access location 120000. 


TEST0:
In the first test, TEST00, we expect the trap to occur after after the
source field. R0 should have advanced by 2 and the low byte of SR1
should hold "20", meaning R0 has been incremented by two.

SIMH:
Test00: mov *(r0)+,(r0)+
Before: R0=120000 SP=744 PC=2064
After:  R0=120002 SP=744 Err=1 SR0=100013 SR1=[0|20] SR2=2064

E11:
Test00: mov *(r0)+,(r0)+
Before: R0=120000 SP=744 PC=2064
After:  R0=120000 SP=744 Err=1 SR0=100013 SR1=[0|0] SR2=2064

As you can see E11 doesn't increment R0 and leaves SR1 null.



TEST01:
In TEST02 the trap occurs on the destination field. SimH is expected
to advance R0 by 4, as shown by the [20|20] SR1.

SIMH:
Test01: mov (r0)+,*(r0)+
Before: R0=117776 SP=744 PC=2266
After:  R0=120002 SP=744 Err=1 SR0=100013 SR1=[20|20] SR2=2266

E11:
Test01: mov (r0)+,*(r0)+
Before: R0=117776 SP=744 PC=2266
After:  R0=117776 SP=744 Err=1 SR0=100013 SR1=[0|0] SR2=2266

E11 backs the instruction out.



TEST02:
This test is much the same as TEST00 and shows that MTPx doesn't push
anything on the stack in case of an error.

SIMH:
Test02: mfpi *(r0)+
Before: R0=120000 SP=744 PC=2462
After:  R0=120002 SP=744 Err=1 SR0=100153 SR1=[0|20] SR2=2462

E11:
Test02: mfpi *(r0)+
Before: R0=120000 SP=744 PC=2462
After:  R0=120000 SP=744 Err=1 SR0=100153 SR1=[0|0] SR2=2462



TEST03:
I was thinking about SR1 tests while was out riding my bike in circles
this evening, and I thought, the most likely place that the E11 tactic
would fail with be with MFPx/MTPx. And that's what happens with MTPI.

SimH correctly shows that both R0 and SP have been incremented with
[20|26]. E11 backs R0 out, but fails to backout SP (it should be 744,
not 746). It's a bug, but probably easily fixed.

SIMH:
Test03: mtpi *(r0)+
Before: R0=120000 SP=744 PC=2700
After:  R0=120002 SP=746 Err=1 SR0=100153 SR1=[20|26] SR2=2700

E11:
Test03: mtpi *(r0)+
Before: R0=120000 SP=744 PC=2700
After:  R0=120000 SP=746 Err=1 SR0=100153 SR1=[0|0] SR2=2700


Now, if only I could my recalcitrant J11 running I could verify all
these tests on real iron.


Ian


