With sticky tape, a pair of tweezers and an ageing RX02 drive I
managed to boot the 11/73. After the RX02 boots I use RUST's ethernet
MOP facility to boot out of a (Windows-native) directory on my Windows
box. The only thing left to fix are the intermittent Winpcap crashes.

Testing was delayed when I decided to use the terminal cable as a trip
rope, pulling out the DLV11J socket and all the little brass things.
An hour later I'd actually managed to put it all back together after
finding the wiring diagrams, straightening pins and those hardware
kind of things one does.  

I've updated the previous tests with J11 status:

